    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">70 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Build it yourself: 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 45 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Coffee Machine</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The machine-coding problem Dunzo made famous and Amazon still asks: drinks are recipes, recipes eat shared ingredients, add-ons like an extra shot or caramel wrap a drink with the Decorator pattern, a Factory builds any combination from a name, and N outlets pour in parallel without ever overselling the milk. You build an all-or-nothing ingredient inventory, a low-stock indicator, refills and a bounded outlet pool. Java, Python and C++14 code all run.</p>\n"
